-- The overworld: the first level, and the only one with a way out of it that
-- is not the exit. The pipe at column 43 is the vault's front door — stand on
-- it and press down.
--
-- Tile names are what the rules collide with, so they are shared across all
-- four levels and only the art differs: `ledge` is turf here and rock in the
-- hollow, and one rule about landing on a ledge covers both.
--
-- `ground` is one row thick and `bedrock` fills in underneath. The hero takes
-- footing from any contact with something it can land on, so a solid slab of
-- ground would be a slab it could jump up the side of — and a gap you can climb
-- out of is not a gap.

tile =  ground   solid  turf.svg
tile _  bedrock  solid  soil.svg
tile -  ledge    solid  sod.svg
tile o  post     solid  stoneblock.svg
tile ^  spikes          spikes.svg
tile P  pipe     solid  pipe.svg
tile *  exit            flag.svg
tile .  air             daylight.svg

map
